<pdd-dependency>brain/library_index_Python.prompt</pdd-dependency>

% Goal

Maintain `brain/scan_library.py` so incremental metadata scans target an explicit database when supplied and otherwise resolve the active collection at call time.

% Contract

R1 (MUST): Resolve the target database once at scan start and use that exact path for the entire scan.
R2 (MUST): Preserve incremental size/mtime skipping, progress state, incomplete-file exclusions, and per-root bulk-removal guards.
R3 (MUST): Store roots and scan state only in the target collection database.
R4 (MUST NOT): A scan must never change registry activation, another collection database, or network/API enrichment state.
R5 (MUST NOT): Missing roots or an unavailable active volume must fail before availability is rewritten.
R6 (MUST): Keep absolute path track identity unchanged and refresh compatibility exports only from the scanned database.

% Output

- Primary output: `brain/scan_library.py`.

% Verification

- Run RED/GREEN focused scan-target and isolation tests plus all existing scan safety tests, then full unittest and py_compile.
